# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore's own reasoning almost exactly (see that file's
# header comment): everything excluded below is either re-created
# automatically by this project's own bootstrap/download logic on first
# use, or is genuinely local/host-only state that must never be baked
# into an image. Keeping the build context small also makes `docker
# build` itself faster -- geper/plugin_model_cache/ alone is ~3.1GB on a
# machine that has already run GEPER once; sending that to the Docker
# daemon on every build (even though a COPY would never reference it)
# would be pure waste.
# =============================================================================

# --- Version control / editor / OS cruft ------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- AI model weights / reference data (auto-downloaded on first use;
#     baked into the image only where explicitly justified in the
#     Dockerfile -- e.g. geper/hyena-dna/'s SOURCE, not its weights) ---------
geper/plugin_model_cache/
geper/hyena-dna/
geper/checkpoints/

# --- Evidence-source local datasets / bulk downloads (auto-bootstrapped) ----
geper/model_cache/

# --- Run output / logs --------------------------------------------------------
geper/geper_output/
geper/logs/
*.log

# --- Docker-related files themselves (no reason for the image to contain
#     its own Dockerfile/compose file) ----------------------------------------
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# --- Local secrets / overrides (must never be baked into an image) ----------
.env
.env.*
geper/config.yaml
!geper/config.yaml.example

# Note: geper/testdata/, geper/testdata_bench/, and the repo-root
# test_data/ are intentionally NOT excluded here (same reasoning
# .gitignore documents) -- they're tiny, purpose-built fixtures, not the
# large re-fetchable caches this file targets, and having them in the
# image is useful for exactly the kind of "does this image actually
# work" smoke test this task's Colab verification will run.
